    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (78.33) and **Trea Turner** (74.00) anchoring the lineup. **Junior Caminero** represents our highest-rated start, buoyed by a highly favorable matchup against Melton (5.22 xERA) and an optimal #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Trea Turner** remains an elite play despite facing a pitcher of Buehler's caliber; his speed and aggressive batting order placement provide high floor efficiency in 5x5 Roto. **Kyle Schwarber** (73.32) rounds out our top-tier trio, benefiting from a prime leadoff opportunity against the same Buehler matchup, keeping his daily output expectations well within the \"Strong\" territory.\n\nStrategic platoon and matchup adjustments heavily influenced our remaining slots. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.03) earns a start despite the projected platoon disadvantage against Jeffrey Springs because his elite sprint speed and #2 lineup projection offer unmatched value in the scarcity-driven SB category. While **Yordan Alvarez** (58.67) faces a stiff test against the elite arm of Paul Skenes (2.93 xERA), his sheer offensive talent and batting order upside make him a mandatory start. Conversely, the most difficult bench decision involved **Luke Raley** (49.08); while he possesses strong platoon splits, his efficiency score fell just short of **Colt Keith** (54.89) and **Caleb Durbin** (56.45). **Luke Raley** remains our primary reserve, but he was edged out today due to his lower overall weighted impact on our target scoring categories compared to the rest of the infield core.\n\nWe continue to monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Christian Yelich**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Should any of these players slide down the order, their efficiency scores will likely compress, necessitating a re-evaluation of our bench depth. **Yordan Alvarez** carries the highest risk today due to the significant SP skill penalty associated with facing Skenes, so we will be watching his early-game at-bats closely to see if he can navigate the difficult matchup to maintain his value.",
